From 6486da4dc7ab4a612f350646cd4b6c017eb2d3c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matterward Labs <admin@matterwardlabs.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 11:53:23 +0530
Subject: point the launcher at the TaffyGo activity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Decision 0024 makes every screen in the screen catalog TaffyGo's, and a
person reaches the first one by tapping the icon. Until this lands the
launcher alias targets ChromeTabbedActivity, so none of the transferred
surfaces is reachable at all.

Two edits in one file. The existing `com.google.android.apps.chrome.Main`
activity-alias is retargeted at TaffyBrowserActivity, and that activity is
declared immediately above it — an alias may only name an activity declared
before it in the manifest, so the position is required rather than tidy.
The declaration takes the `chrome_activity_common` block for its
`hardwareAccelerated="false"` posture: TaffyGo's activity is not derived
from ChromeActivity, but it hosts the same compositor, so the note above
`application_definitions()` applies for the same reason rather than by
inheritance. The alias stays exported because a launcher alias must be;
the target activity remains non-exported.

This patch carried a third edit until 2026-09-20: a closed `VIEW`/`BROWSABLE`
filter on the same alias for `com.taffygo.browser://auth`, the account
plane's OAuth return. Decision 0200 removed the account plane's servers and
the ingress that read that intent went with it, so the filter named a URI no
code in the product resolves and no flow can emit. It is removed here rather
than in a patch of its own, because a queue that adds a filter and then
withdraws it is two numbers describing one thing that never shipped. Provider
sign-in is unaffected and never used this road: a vendor's redirect is
claimed by a navigation throttle inside the errand page (decision 0095), not
delivered as an Android intent.

The manifest is a jinja template and this block is not parameterised — the
`{% if %}` conditions nearby govern channel-specific categories inside the
launcher intent filter, not the alias or its target — so there is no
downstream value to set. A manifest merger cannot retarget an existing alias
either: merging adds and overlays elements, and the launcher category would
be declared twice, pointing at two activities.

ChromeTabbedActivity keeps its upstream declaration because Chromium still has
explicit internal callers. It is not a TaffyGo product entry point.

Owner: TaffyGo browser shell.
Retirement: permanent, reviewed at each milestone rebase. It retires only if
upstream ever parameterises the launcher alias's target, which would make it
mechanism D in decision 0024 and cost no patch.

Taffy-Patch: 0022

diff --git a/chrome/android/java/AndroidManifest.xml b/chrome/android/java/AndroidManifest.xml
index 96fac0c552827..bc03777611088 100644
--- a/chrome/android/java/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/chrome/android/java/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -637,8 +637,17 @@ by a child template that "extends" this file.
             <property android:name="android.window.PROPERTY_SUPPORTS_MULTI_INSTANCE_SYSTEM_UI"
                 android:value="true" />
         </activity>
+        <!-- TaffyGo: the activity the launcher alias below targets. An alias may
+             only name an activity declared before it, so this block sits here
+             rather than beside the other downstream code. -->
+        <activity android:name="org.chromium.taffy.shell.TaffyBrowserActivity"
+            android:theme="@style/Theme.Chromium.TabbedMode"
+            android:exported="false"
+            android:launchMode="singleTask"
+            {{ self.chrome_activity_common() }}>
+        </activity>
         <activity-alias android:name="com.google.android.apps.chrome.Main"
-            android:targetActivity="org.chromium.chrome.browser.ChromeTabbedActivity"
+            android:targetActivity="org.chromium.taffy.shell.TaffyBrowserActivity"
             android:exported="true">
             <property android:name="android.window.PROPERTY_SUPPORTS_MULTI_INSTANCE_SYSTEM_UI"
                 android:value="true" />
